1. Definitions
--------------

"Covered Software" means source code, documentation, and other material
that expressly identifies this License as governing it.

"Covered File" means a source or documentation file that is part of the
Covered Software.

"Modification" means a change to a Covered File or a new file that is
substantially derived from a Covered File.

"Port" means a Modification whose purpose includes enabling the Covered
Software to build, run, integrate, or interoperate on another operating
system, architecture, runtime, API, or platform.

"Executable Form" means any form other than the preferred form for making
modifications.

"Larger Work" means a work that combines Covered Software with separate
material not governed by this License.

"Contributor" means a copyright holder who intentionally submits or
distributes a Modification under this License.

"Upstream Project" means a pre-existing project expressly identified in
the Covered Software's provenance metadata as the project from which a
Covered Software component was derived.

